  title: British Singapura
  info: 'In 1819, British statesman Stamford Raffles arrived in Singapura and struck
    a deal with locals to make Singapore a free trading port. The Dutch had blocked
    off all trade in that area, and the British wanted to make Singapore''s port
    free to encourage trade. By 1871, Singapore''s population had reached nearly
    100,000. '
